  "title": "Floodplain Seed Cooperative",
  "rules": [
    "Twenty-four households share a serpentine watershed. All 96 people have native actions; livestock and trays are separate objects.",
    "Sow a seed, then apply hoe and watering care. Wet and dry crops have distinct moisture/salt limits; orchards grow half as often.",
    "Harvest needs a sickle and nearby Assist. Private food, seed donation and levee repair compete for each harvest bundle.",
    "A sluice sends up to two water and one salt units downstream after three subsequent transitions. The final household drains outside the world.",
    "Boat users launch trays. Wet open source gates move trays through three increments to the next nursery; neighbors can collect the real seed.",
    "Herd livestock to barns before floods. Safe livestock and fallow fields restore soil. Food consumption and flood damage are native state. Season ends at 896."
  ],
